name>Welt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Real</surname><given-names>FX</given-names></name><name><surname>Rettig</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Old</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organ-specific expression of the colon cancer antigen A33, a cell surface target for antibody-based therapy</article-title><source>Int J Oncol</source><year>1996</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>471</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Oncol||9|465||bib10|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ireton</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>McDermott</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Black</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoddard</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The structure of <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> cytosine deaminase</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>315</volume><fpage>687</fpage><lpage>697</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Mol Biol||315|687||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11812140</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rader</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nathan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Elia</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gout</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Jungbluth</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name><name><surname>Welt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Old</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Barbas III</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The rabbit antibody repertoire as a novel source for the generation of therapeutic human antibodies</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>13668</fpage><lpage>13676</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||275|13668||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10788485</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wallace</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>MacMaster</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>VF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerr</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Senter</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Cosand</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intratumoral generation of 5-fluorouracil mediated by an antibody &#x02013; cytosine deaminase conjugate in combination with 5-fluorocytosine</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1994</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>2719</fpage><lpage>2723</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||54|2719||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8168103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webley</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Francis</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pedley</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharma</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Begent</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartley</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hochhauser</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measurement of the critical DNA lesions produced by antibody-directed enzyme prodrug therapy (ADEPT) <italic>in vitro</italic>, <italic>in vivo</italic> and in clinical material</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>1671</fpage><lpage>1676</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||84|1671||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11401322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Welt</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Divgi</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemeny</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Finn</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Daghighian</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Germain</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Old</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phase I&#x0002f;II study of iodine 125-labeled monoclonal antibody A33 in patients with advanced colon cancer</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1996</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>1787</fpage><lpage>1797</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||14|1787||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8656247</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>